  "supersedes": "assessment-v1.0.1",
  "changes": [
    "assessment_rules.json scoring.tier_profile: sentence 2 restated. The prose read 'the highest tier observed at secure, or if none, the highest tier observed at emerging', which for developing secure plus stretch emerging yields developing_secure. Fixture FX-STRETCH requires stretch_emerging, and every other fixture agrees with it. The implementation followed the fixtures; the prose now says what they mean. No item, key, fixture or score changes.",
    "assessment_rules.json scoring.secure_threshold (0.75) and scoring.emerging_threshold (0.50) added. The values were stated only inside the tier_profile prose, so the scoring module carried its own copy of them as constants. They are now data the module reads."
  ]
